  "body": "Moved from https://github.com/vector-im/element-web/issues/3983\r\nRelated https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/issues/6735\r\nRelated https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/issues/6346\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\n> trying to access #testingGuest:matrix.org as a guest from the directory gives the error message '#testingGuest:matrix.org does not exist'. Whatever is the reason for this msg to appear (deleted alias? not accessible to guests?) should be managed in a much nicer way: if something is missing the room should not be in the directory.\r\n\r\n> ok I think the bottom line is that the address was removed => when removing the only address of a room there should be a warning saying \"we will unlist it\" and actually unlist it\r\n\r\n> I found this room again, added an address (#testingguestaccess:matrix.org) but not selected it in the drop down (the first added address should be selected by default in the drop down). I was able to join this address directly but still not from the directory.\r\n\r\n> I got back, selected the new address (#testingguestaccess:matrix.org) in the drop down and the wrong one (#testingGuest:matrix.org was displayed in the browser.\r\n\r\nNote accessible may mean knockable, accessible to a space member, invited, or publicly joinable.\r\n\r\n",
